\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Two geometries and the retained functional}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{The cylinder ultrametric of \ref{fdip-00FE} is defined for
every integer #{p\ge 2}, with no reference to #{\lambda}. The
increment ultrametric of \ref{fdip-00FI} additionally
requires #{0<p\lambda<1}, and its covering sums are computed
in \ref{fdip-00FK}. For #{p\lambda\ge 1}, \ref{fdip-00FL}
excludes a square-integrable point density with the cell
averages #{F_k}, while \ref{fdip-00C3} still supplies the
finitely additive ball assignment. The convergence in
\ref{fdip-00FM} holds for every #{\lambda>0} because the
hypotheses of \ref{fdip-00C6} already do. The critical order
in \ref{fdip-00FK} is the [Hausdorff dimension](fdip-00D5) of
#{(X,d)}.}
